– is associated with social inhibition across a 2-year period and is also associated with a different pattern of cardiac reactivity."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The stated replication goals explicitly name this original; the overall verdict supports dysregulated fear and its longitudinal association with inhibition. Differences in curve modeling and new RSA analyses do not reverse this verdict.""}"
10.1002/jaba.659,4778452caf8b412e,0,10.1016/j.lmot.2017.02.003,Clinical applications of procedures to promote the emergence of untrained intraverbal relations with children with autism.,"Shillingsburg, M. A., Frampton, S. E., Cleveland, S. A., & Cariveau, T.",2018,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Shillingsburg, M. A., Frampton, S. E., Cleveland, S. A., & Cariveau, T."", ""year"": ""2018"", ""title"": ""Clinical applications of procedures to promote the emergence of untrained intraverbal relations with children with autism."", ""doi"": ""10.1016/j.lmot.2017.02.003"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Shillingsburg, Frampton, Cleveland, and Cariveau (2018) taught listener and tact by feature, name-feature intraverbal, and feature-name intraverbal responses across sets and reported emergence of responses that were not directly trained for 6 individuals diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder (ASD). The current study was a systematic replication with the addition of instructive feedback (IF) with 2 children diagnosed with ASD."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""We observed increased correct responses for related verbal responses; replicating Shillingsburg et al."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Abstract explicitly states replication of the earlier trained/untrained verbal-response finding. Target citation copied from publisher reference list.""}"
10.3390/su12083069,5d6d78606263c6ee,0,10.1108/BFJ-04-2017-0255,Assessment of household food waste in Hungary,"Szabó-Bódi, B.; Kasza, G.; Szakos, D.",2018,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Szabó-Bódi, B.; Kasza, G.; Szakos, D."", ""year"": ""2018"", ""title"": ""Assessment of household food waste in Hungary"", ""doi"": ""10.1108/BFJ-04-2017-0255"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""The actual study is a replication of the first Hungarian measurement-based research conducted in 2016 [24], which we regarded as a baseline for comparison."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The constitution of food waste in the households was found to be very similar, indicating a dominant rate of avoidable food waste (an actual share of 48.82% compared to 48.70% in 2016), followed by the unavoidable part (47.05% compared to 47.13% in 2016). Potentially avoidable food waste remained under 5% in both periods."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors explicitly compare the repeated national measurement with the baseline and report very similar composition and the same ranking of discarded foods. The small temporal decrease is interpreted as campaign progress, not failure of the earlier finding. FUSIONS is a methodology source, not another target.""}"
10.7554/elife.73430,58f7736b9d35d428,0,10.1016/j.cell.2010.02.027,A chromatin-mediated reversible drug-tolerant state in cancer cell subpopulations,Sharma SV Lee DY Li B Quinlan MP Takahashi F Maheswaran S McDermott U Azizian N Zou L Fischbach MA Wong KK Brandstetter K Wittner B Ramaswamy S Classon M Settleman J,2010,full_text,,error,argon,"{""target_index"": 0, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""verdict"": ""blind_right"", ""corrected_value"": {""doi"": ""10.1016/j.cell.2010.02.027"", ""title"": ""A chromatin-mediated reversible drug-tolerant state in cancer cell subpopulations"", ""authors"": ""Sharma SV Lee DY Li B Quinlan MP Takahashi F Maheswaran S McDermott U Azizian N Zou L Fischbach MA Wong KK Brandstetter K Wittner B Ramaswamy S Classon M Settleman J"", ""year"": ""2010"", ""type"": ""replication"", ""outcome"": ""uninformative""}, ""quote"": ""As part of the Reproducibility Project: Cancer Biology, we published a Registered Report ( Haven et al., 2016 ) that described how we intended to replicate selected experiments from the paper ‘A chromatin-mediated reversible drug-tolerant state in cancer cell subpopulations’ ( Sharma et al., 2010 ). We attempted to independently replicate experiments that tested the phenotype of a small subpopulation of ‘drug-tolerant persister’ cells (DTPs) that are generated when PC9 cells, a protein-tyrosine kinase inhibitor (TKI)-sensitive non-small cell lung cancer cell line, is exposed to high concentrations of TKIs."", ""location"": ""Results — Partial replication: a chromatin-mediated reversible drug-tolerant state in cancer cell subpopulations"", ""reason"": ""Omitted target: this paper reports new experimental replication data (Figure 1, Materials and methods, OSF dataset) re-testing Sharma et al. (2010), with an explicit uninformative outcome summary stating that the preliminary data do not address the central claim because the remaining experiments were not continued.""}","{""authors"": ""Sharma SV Lee DY Li B Quinlan MP Takahashi F Maheswaran S McDermott U Azizian N Zou L Fischbach MA Wong KK Brandstetter K Wittner B Ramaswamy S Classon M Settleman J"", ""year"": ""2010"", ""title"": ""A chromatin-mediated reversible drug-tolerant state in cancer cell subpopulations"", ""doi"": ""10.1016/j.cell.2010.02.027"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""As part of the Reproducibility Project: Cancer Biology, we published a Registered Report ( Haven et al., 2016 ) that described how we intended to replicate selected experiments from the paper ‘A chromatin-mediated reversible drug-tolerant state in cancer cell subpopulations’ ( Sharma et al., 2010 )."", ""outcome"": ""uninformative"", ""outcome_quote"": ""To summarize, this replication attempt obtained preliminary outcomes although the experiments were not continued and thus these data do not address whether DTPs maintained viability through IGF-1 receptor signaling and an altered chromatin state dependent on the histone demethylase KDM5A."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors explicitly report inability to adjudicate the central finding."", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """"}"
