association is accompanied by an explicit contrast: no female association and/or no stronger centenarian association.""}"
10.1111/j.1474-9726.2010.00627.x,22bd1fb37b70c337,4,,Association of common genetic variation in the insulin ⁄ IGF1 signaling pathway with human longevity,"Pawlikowska L, Hu D, Huntsman S, Sung A, Chu C, Chen J, Joyner AH, Schork NJ, Hsueh WC, Reiner AP, Psaty BM, Atzmon G, Barzilai N, Cummings SR, Browner WS, Kwok PY, Ziv E",2009,full_text,,error,argon,"{""target_index"": 4, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""verdict"": ""blind_right"", ""corrected_value"": {""doi"": """", ""title"": ""Association of common genetic variation in the insulin ⁄ IGF1 signaling pathway with human longevity"", ""authors"": ""Pawlikowska L, Hu D, Huntsman S, Sung A, Chu C, Chen J, Joyner AH, Schork NJ, Hsueh WC, Reiner AP, Psaty BM, Atzmon G, Barzilai N, Cummings SR, Browner WS, Kwok PY, Ziv E"", ""year"": ""2009""}, ""quote"": ""Four of them (rs13217795, rs2764264, rs479744, and rs9400239) have previously been reported to be associated (after correction for multiple testing) in at least one study (Flachsbart et al. 2009;Willcox et al. 2008), whereas three SNPs (rs13220810, 7762395, rs9486902) have been shown to be nominally significant (Flachsbart et al. 2009;Pawlikowska et al. 2009)."", ""location"": ""Discussion, line 26"", ""reason"": ""Omitted target: the paper directly re-tests the tagging SNP associations reported by Pawlikowska et al. (2009) and compares its allele, genotype, and sex-stratified results against them.""}","{""authors"": ""Pawlikowska L, Hu D, Huntsman S, Sung A, Chu C, Chen J, Joyner AH, Schork NJ, Hsueh WC, Reiner AP, Psaty BM, Atzmon G, Barzilai N, Cummings SR, Browner WS, Kwok PY, Ziv E"", ""year"": ""2009"", ""title"": ""Association of common genetic variation in the insulin ⁄ IGF1 signaling pathway with human longevity"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""First, we conducted case-control analyses and found [as seen in previous studies (Anselmi et al."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""No nominally significant effects (either by PCCA or PCCG) were found for the females.\nTo correct for multiple testing, while taking into account the LD between the individual SNPs, permutation analysis was performed using the Plink software."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The original association is described as female-specific; the present study finds no female associations.""}"
10.1080/14719037.2017.1282000,f47e46981f1f5369,0,,,Van Ryzin,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Van Ryzin"", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""description"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2, 3"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Van Ryzin experimentally manipulated expectations and performance and found a direct effect of performance, but no disconfirmation. We performed: an exact replication; a conceptual replication with extreme manipulations; a conceptual replication that reversed the order of a performance and expectations manipulation."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Study 1 and 2 reproduced original findings. In contrast, study 3 indicates that expectation cues are retrospectively used to anchor prior experiences of performance."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Two replications agree, while the third is explicitly contrasted. Original bibliographic entry unavailable in abstract.""}"
10.1177/1948550618775410,05781ebeec482e07,1,10.1037/aca0000069,Different stories: How levels of familiarity with literary and genre fiction relate to mentalizing.,"Kidd, D., & Castano, E.",2017a,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Kidd, D., & Castano, E."", ""year"": ""2017a"", ""title"": ""Different stories: How levels of familiarity with literary and genre fiction relate to mentalizing."", ""doi"": ""10.1037/aca0000069"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1, 2, 3"", ""evidence_quote"": ""More broadly, these experimental effects align well with the documented positive relation between lifetime experience with literary fiction (but not popular genre fiction) and ToM reported by Kidd and Castano (2017a) and replicated in each of the three present studies."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""More broadly, these experimental effects align well with the documented positive relation between lifetime experience with literary fiction (but not popular genre fiction) and ToM reported by Kidd and Castano (2017a) and replicated in each of the three present studies."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors explicitly characterize the aggregate outcome for this target.""}"
10.1177/0956797618761661,089bc93ae014e8a3,1,,The nature of adolescent competencies predicted by preschool delay of gratification.,"Mischel W., Shoda Y., Peake P. K.",1988,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Mischel W., Shoda Y., Peake P. K."", ""year"": ""1988"", ""title"": ""The nature of adolescent competencies predicted by preschool delay of gratification."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""We attempted to extend the famous findings of Mischel and Shoda (\nMischel et al., 1988\n;\nMischel et al., 1989\n;\nShoda et al., 1990\n) by examining associations between early delay of gratification and adolescent outcomes in a more diverse sample of children and with more sophisticated statistical models."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""We attempted to extend the famous findings of Mischel and Shoda (\nMischel et al., 1988\n;\nMischel et al., 1989\n;\nShoda et al., 1990\n) by examining associations between early delay of gratification and adolescent outcomes in a more diverse sample of children and with more sophisticated statistical models. As with the earlier studies, we found statistically significant, although smaller, bivariate associations between early delay ability and later achievement. But we also found that these associations were highly sensitive to the inclusion of controls. Moreover, we failed to find even bivariate associations between delay of gratification at age 54 months and a host of behavioral outcomes at age 15, which was remarkable given the stability in self-control measures found in other studies (e.g.,\nMoffitt et al., 2011\n)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Authors compare the longitudinal findings as a set: academic associations agree, behavioral associations do not. Reduced magnitude alone is not the basis for mixed.""}"
10.1037/pspa0000121,0ebf1107d4b56633,1,10.1177/1745691616674458,"Registered replication report: Strack, Martin, & Stepper (1988).","Wagenmakers, E.-J., Beek, T., Dijkhoff, L., Gronau, Q. F., Acosta, A., Adams, R. B., Jr.,... Zwaan, R. A.",2016,full_text,,error,argon,"{""target_index"": 1, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""verdict"": ""blind_right"", ""corrected_value"": {""doi"": ""10.1177/1745691616674458"", ""title"": ""Registered replication report: Strack, Martin, & Stepper (1988)."", ""authors"": ""Wagenmakers, E.-J., Beek, T., Dijkhoff, L., Gronau, Q. F., Acosta, A., Adams, R. B., Jr.,... Zwaan, R. A."", ""year"": ""2016"", ""type"": ""replication"", ""outcome"": ""successful""}, ""quote"": ""However, in the present work we sought to compare the outcomes of the two specific procedures that were used in past studies, one by Strack et al. (1988) and the other by Wagenmakers et al. (2016), and therefore, we repeated the same procedures that were used in those studies."", ""location"": ""Discussion, p. 660"", ""reason"": ""Omitted target: the paper explicitly repeats the camera-present procedure of Wagenmakers et al. (2016) to re-test its reported null finding and confirms the absence of the facial-feedback effect when a camera is present.""}","{""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""However, in the present work we sought to compare the outcomes of the two specific procedures that were used in past studies, one by Strack et al. (1988) and the other by Wagenmakers et al. (2016), and therefore, we repeated the same procedures that were used in those studies."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Our results suggest that the original findings of a facial feedback effect (Strack et al., 1988) and the null effect in the replication studies (Wagenmakers et al., 2016) are not contradictory: The facial-feedback effect was present when the camera was absent and participants were not concerned with performance monitoring; The effect diminished when the participants’ performance was recorded and participants were warned that their performance was being monitored."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""authors"": ""Wagenmakers, E.-J., Beek, T., Dijkhoff, L., Gronau, Q. F., Acosta, A., Adams, R. B., Jr.,... Zwaan, R. A."", ""year"": ""2016"", ""title"": ""Registered replication report: Strack, Martin, & Stepper (1988)."", ""doi"": ""10.1177/1745691616674458"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The camera condition repeats and confirms the null finding in the published replication project; this is an explicit target, not only a source of materials.""}"
10.5465/amproc.2023.222bp,74dd15ebcf49077e,0,,,"Pe’er, Vertinsky and Keil",2016,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Pe’er, Vertinsky and Keil"", ""year"": ""2016"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Pe’er, Vertinsky and Keil, Strategic Management Journal, 2016, 37, 541–564, provide empirical evidence for an inverted-U shaped relationship between venture growth and survival. We replicate their study and extend it by distinguishing between exit and failure, addressing the assumptions of survival modelling, and examining potential reverse causality due to the notion that the prospect of failure may spur firms to downsize (temporarily) - a phenomenon referred to as the shadow of death. Even though we obtain nearly identical results when performing an exact replication of Pe’er et al.’s study, the findings of our extension reveal a relationship between growth and survival that is the exact opposite of what earlier growth-survival studies including Pe’er et al. (2016) have found."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Even though we obtain nearly identical results when performing an exact replication of Pe’er et al.’s study, the findings of our extension reveal a relationship between growth and survival that is the exact opposite of what earlier growth-survival studies including Pe’er et al. (2016) have found."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Exact replication agrees but the extension explicitly reverses the original relationship. The abstract does not expose the original title or DOI.""}"
10.1123/jsep.2025-0001,674b7c400fdbc099,0,,,,2019,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": ""2019"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""In a replication and extension of this study, we wanted to find out whether its findings replicate in a sample of 1,718 observations from 1,270 U.S. college athletes and whether effort expenditure is driven by working in a team or the chance of valuable outcomes in the relay."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""As shown by linear mixed modeling and regression analyses, runners exhibited effort gains only if their relays had high medal chances and if they had not been successful in the individual competition (i.e., did not place first to third). Moreover, relay members who had been successful in the individual competition showed effort losses."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Original effort gains are stated and the replication finds them only under restricted conditions, with losses in others; provisionally mixed. Complete reference entry is not present in the saved abstract; no citation metadata guessed.""}"
10.1073/pnas.2103313118,643e1bb7a06e2a12,7,,,Fernbach; Kan; Lynch,2015,full_text,,error,argon,"{""target_index"": 7, ""field"": ""missing_row"", ""method"": ""argon"", ""verdict"": ""blind_right"", ""corrected_value"": {""doi"": """", ""title"": """", ""authors"": ""Fernbach; Kan; Lynch"", ""year"": ""2015"", ""type"": ""replication"", ""outcome"": ""mixed""}, ""quote"": ""Study 2 of Fernbach, Kan, and Lynch 2015 contains two primary predictions and analyses. This study manipulated the level of financial constraint and asked participants to provide their strategy to address the constraint."", ""location"": ""PRIMARY PROJECT REPORT: Fernbach (line 564)"", ""reason"": ""Omitted target: Fernbach, Kan, & Lynch (2015), Study 2 is one of the 20 studies replicated in O'Donnell et al. (2021), documented in the Fernbach project report, Table A, and the project spreadsheet, but omitted from the 17 shipped rows.""}","{""authors"": ""Fernbach; Kan; Lynch"", ""year"": ""2015"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": ""2"", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Study 2 of Fernbach, Kan, and Lynch 2015 contains two primary predictions and analyses."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In the replication, there was no interaction of constraint and plan type on planning mix, F(1,222) = 0.29, p = .752. In testing for response times, there was an interaction of constraint and plan time on log-transformed response time, F(2, 299) = 3.04, p = .049."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The project report compares failure of the original planning-mix finding and a significant response-time interaction. An added model matching the original fails too; no overall verdict overrides the reported partly agreeing comparisons. Full title and author initials unavailable in acquired text.""}"
