 false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Original central interaction is null in primary spreadsheet (r=-0.03, 95% CI [-0.11133135,0.04324818]); replication interaction is also null. Agreement is successful even without significance. Lower confidence because the narrative does not explicitly compare its null with the original null and project date labels disagree; full citation in write-up says 2018, summary says 2019.""}"
10.3758/s13423-021-01927-8,fb476f6a733a7e47,0,,The action–sentence compatibility effect: It's all in the timing.,"Borreggine, K. L., & Kaschak, M. P.",2006,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Borreggine, K. L., & Kaschak, M. P."", ""year"": ""2006"", ""title"": ""The action–sentence compatibility effect: It's all in the timing."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""As a first step in assessing the replicability of motor compatibility effects, we conducted a pre-registered, multi-lab replication of the ACE. We used an adapted version of the original ACE paradigm (Glenberg & Kaschak, 2002) that was used in Borreggine and Kaschak (2006)."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""The results of the replication effort are clear: This version of the ACE was not statistically significant in any of the individual studies, and the meta-analytic effect size was close to zero (see Fig. 6)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The overall verdict is a clear failure for this version of ACE in all 18 labs, with a near-zero pooled effect.""}"
10.5539/ibr.v5n4p71,8c158b1f567dad84,0,,,"Hofstede, G.",1980,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Hofstede, G."", ""year"": ""1980"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""This study replicates Hofstede’s study with data obtained from students studying for their master degrees in different universities in Jordan."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In conclusion we argue that Hofstede’s (1980, 1991, 2005) assumption that people who grow up in the same place will share similar views about life does not apply to his findings about Arab cultures and thus his generalization made to Jordanian culture is not validated."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The overall conclusion rejects the generalization to Jordan, which decides the verdict despite agreement on some dimensions.""}"
