10.1167/18.10.139,8b38dc8bb390979b,0,,,Moran et al.,2017,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Moran et al."", ""year"": ""2017"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Moran et al. (2017, VSS) found that realistic miniature increased immersion relative to unrealistic miniatures, but memory was unaffected. However, the questions used to assess memory were very easy, raising the possibility of a ceiling effect. The current experiment was very similar to Moran et al. (2017)."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""However, immersion results failed to replicate: immersion scores did not significantly differ across the three conditions."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The title focuses on immersion and this effect explicitly failed. The prior memory null was also recovered; under the title-specific coding rule the central immersion finding is failed. The directly repeated study is Moran et al. (2017), not the earlier Baranowski and Hecht paper. No reference list is available to expand the citation.""}"
10.17605/osf.io/r8qp2,8109f7a62fdc044f,1,10.1177/0261927X12460666,The Language of Political Aggression,"Matsumoto, D., & Hwang, H. C.",2013,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Matsumoto, D., & Hwang, H. C."", ""year"": ""2013"", ""title"": ""The Language of Political Aggression"", ""doi"": ""10.1177/0261927X12460666"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1A, 1B, 2A, 2B, 3"", ""evidence_quote"": ""We sought to conceptually replicate two studies of the role of linguistic style in\n\npredicting war attitudes and behaviors, Abe (2012) and Matsumoto and Hwang (2013), in\n\nthe U.S. Congressional context."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""We add to this area by replicating two\n\nprevious studies: Abe (2012) and Matsumoto and Hwang (2013) in the context of a\n\nlegislative body. The present study hypothesized that legislators who support war measures\n\nwould be externally focused and less cognitively complex in their speeches, while opponents\n\nof war measures would be internally focused. Speeches were obtained pertaining to the\n\ndecisions for the U.S. to take military action in Kosovo, Iraq, and Libya. While we found\n\nmixed results depending on the circumstances of a speciﬁc conﬂict, we demonstrate how\n\nautomated language analysis can be combined with voting records to better understand\n\nbehavioral action, such as legislative decision."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract explicitly frames the combined conceptual replications as mixed across conflicts; results and discussion report supported and unsupported hypotheses across samples.""}"
10.7287/peerj.preprints.804v1,2558baa058315658,0,,,,2013,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": ""2013"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""A study by White et al. found that population disease burden predicted preference for attractive politicians in U.S. congressional elections. Aim: We aimed to replicate this finding using data from the United Kingdom."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""None of the health metrics predicted rated sexiness of members of parliament."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The original association is explicitly described and the corresponding UK analysis found none. Target bibliography unavailable; do not import it from the later published version.""}"
10.1167/15.14.1,f2188a45e3b6d8c4,0,10.1016/j.visres.2009.01.006,Low-level features determine brightness in White’s and Benary’s illusions.,"Salmela, V. R., & Laurinen, P. I.",2009,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Salmela, V. R., & Laurinen, P. I."", ""year"": ""2009"", ""title"": ""Low-level features determine brightness in White’s and Benary’s illusions."", ""doi"": ""10.1016/j.visres.2009.01.006"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""We replicated and extended Salmela and Laurinen’s (2009) results, and\n     tested a number of diferent multi-scale spatial iltering models with respect to\n     their capability to reproduce the psychophysically observed efects of narrow-\n     band noise on lightness perception."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Still, despite these diiculties with interpreting precisely what the\n     lightness matches mean, the data consistently demonstrate that for most ob-\n     servers, noise in the range from 1 to 5 cpd has the largest efect on perceived\n     lightness, and that the most efective noise frequency does not scale propor-\n     tionally to the grating frequency."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The stated original noise-masking finding is observed again: strongest masking from 1 to 5 cpd. Tests of theoretical models with new stimuli are not reanalyses of original data.""}"
10.1080/14719037.2016.1195009,9a8a1255550022be,0,10.1111/puar.12401,Representative Bureaucracy and the Willingness to Coproduce: An Experimental Study.,"Riccucci, N. M., G. G. Van Ryzin, and H. Li.",2016,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Riccucci, N. M., G. G. Van Ryzin, and H. Li."", ""year"": ""2016"", ""title"": ""Representative Bureaucracy and the Willingness to Coproduce: An Experimental Study."", ""doi"": ""10.1111/puar.12401"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""The purpose of this study is to conceptually replicate an earlier study by Riccucci, Van Ryzin, and Li (2016), who examined the effects of representative bureaucracy on the public’s willingness to participate with government in recycling."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Our experiment, in sum, produced only null findings, in contrast to the original study by Riccucci, Van Ryzin, and Li (2016)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true}"
10.1002/hrdq.21464,4866281e6326e57b,0,,"Job attitudes and employee engagement: Considering the ""A-factor"".","Newman, D. A., Joseph, D. L., & Hulin, C. L.",2010,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Newman, D. A., Joseph, D. L., & Hulin, C. L."", ""year"": ""2010"", ""title"": ""Job attitudes and employee engagement: Considering the \""A-factor\""."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""For the relationships among work engagement, job satisfaction, affective organizational commitment, and job involvement, we used the meta-analytic correlations from Newman et al. (2010). This allowed us to replicate and extend the work of Newman et al. by conducting new analyses on the same data."", ""outcome"": """", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": ""computationally reproducible"", ""outcome_computational_quote"": ""For example, our model produced estimated latent correlations from the A-factor of job attitudes to work engagement (φ=0.77), job satisfaction (φ=0.71), affective organizational commitment (φ=0.75), and job involvement (φ=0.72) that were identical to those reported by Newman et al. (2010). Only the RMSEA values differed slightly where our analysis yielded a value 0.006 lower than the value of 0.180 reported by Newman."", ""outcome_robustness"": ""robustness challenges"", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": ""Therefore, interpretation of relationships between factors such as those made by Newman et al. (2010) –and others –require analyses similar to those reported in the present study."", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Original meta-analytic data reanalysed with variance decomposition, challenging redundancy interpretation. Original 2010 numerical model explicitly recovered up to minor fit-index variation; numerical reproduction of 2011 is not separately established. Both publications are directly re-examined; 2010 supplied the data and original numerical model, while 2011 states the challenged claim. Partial full-text extraction limits certainty, especially the scope of the 2010 robustness verdict.""}"
10.1371/journal.pone.0126363,5e91a20ae553fe8f,0,10.1038/ng.2383,Large-scale association analysis provides insights into the genetic architecture and pathophysiology of type 2 diabetes,"Morris AP, Voight BF, Teslovich TM, Ferreira T, Segrè AV, Steinthorsdottir V, et al.",2012,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Morris AP, Voight BF, Teslovich TM, Ferreira T, Segrè AV, Steinthorsdottir V, et al."", ""year"": ""2012"", ""title"": ""Large-scale association analysis provides insights into the genetic architecture and pathophysiology of type 2 diabetes"", ""doi"": ""10.1038/ng.2383"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""We selected 10 autosomal SNPs identified by European GWAS in 2012, including, rs12571751 in ZMIZ1, rs10842994 near KLHDC5, rs2796441 near TLE1, rs459193 near ANKRD55, rs10401969 in CILP2, rs12970134 near MC4R, rs7202877 near BCAR1, rs11063069 near CCND2, rs8108269 near GIPR [16], and rs8090011 in LAMA1 [15]."", ""outcome"": ""mixed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In this study, we examined the association of 7 SNPs, rs12571751 in ZMIZ1, rs10842994 near KLHDC5, rs2796441 near TLE1, rs459193 near ANKRD55, rs10401969 in CILP2, rs12970134 near MC4R, and rs7202877 near BCAR1, with susceptibility to type 2 diabetes in a Japanese population, and found that rs12571751 in ZMIZ1 was significantly associated with type 2 diabetes in the Japanese population. We also examined the effects of 3 additional SNP loci, rs11063069 near CCND2 and rs8108269 near GIPR, which were identified in sex-differentiated analyses [16], and rs8090011 in LAMA1, which was shown to be associated with non-obese type 2 diabetes in European GWAS [15], but we did not replicate the original association in the Japanese population (Tables 4 and 5, S3 Table)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true}"
10.17605/osf.io/8wd2b,c20f9db39f03cdd4,0,,Do defaults save lives?,"Johnson, E. J., & Goldstein, D.",2003,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Johnson, E. J., & Goldstein, D."", ""year"": ""2003"", ""title"": ""Do defaults save lives?"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": ""Experiment 1"", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""In two well-powered samples (N = 1920), we conducted a close replication of the default effect in Johnson and Goldstein (2003) and in Johnson, Bellman, and Lohse (2002)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""We successfully replicated Johnson and Goldstein (2003)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Overall verdict confirms this target despite smaller effects; both samples contributed to Part 1.""}"
10.17605/osf.io/8wd2b,c20f9db39f03cdd4,2,,,Van Dalen and Henkens,2014,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Van Dalen and Henkens"", ""year"": ""2014"", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""We based our extension on Van Dalen and Henkens (2014) who found that organ donation rates were higher when the option was temporary and would have to be renewed than when the default option was to donate."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In the first extension, we predicted that people would be more inclined to become donors when consent to organ donation is temporary. We found no evidence that consent varied between the temporary and permanent conditions."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Extension 1 explicitly retests this cited temporal-choice finding in Sample 1. The supplied cache lacks its reference entry; title and DOI cannot be copied.""}"
10.1371/journal.pone.0246058,58d96ab64c094730,1,,Mitigation system threat partially mediates the effects of right-wing ideologies on climate change beliefs.,"Clarke EJ, Ling M, Kothe EJ, Klas A, Richardson B.",2019,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Clarke EJ, Ling M, Kothe EJ, Klas A, Richardson B."", ""year"": ""2019"", ""title"": ""Mitigation system threat partially mediates the effects of right-wing ideologies on climate change beliefs."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""When pitted against each other, we replicate recent findings that of these dimensions, SDO-E and Traditionalism demonstrate strongest unique associations with environmentalism [62]."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""When pitted against each other, we replicate recent findings that of these dimensions, SDO-E and Traditionalism demonstrate strongest unique associations with environmentalism [62]."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors explicitly state replication of this original paper’s finding about the strongest unique ideological associations. This is an additional retested finding in the exploratory analyses.""}"
10.30707/etd2019.george.a,f5cd9ebc971eb837,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Our research replicates a previous study, which examined how Christians being led to believe God will either include or exclude them influenced well-being scores."", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The abstract confirms the exclusion hypothesis but also reports an absent moderation; it gives neither the original results nor an overall replication verdict. It therefore cannot settle agreement across the original findings.""}"
10.1891/jcop.2005.19.4.309,63030915d136ccf9,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Research to date suggests that the best treatment for many mental disorders is provided through the combination of medications and psychotherapy (e.g., Hollon, Thase, & Markowitz, 2002). However, the majority of studies supporting this point have been done utilizing highly restricted, controlled samples that may not accurately reflect the way mental illness is treated in the community. The present study attempted to replicate those findings in an outpatient community clinic."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Results showed that clients who took medications fared no better than clients who did not. These preliminary findings suggest that the combination of medications and psychotherapy may not be as effective in the “real world” as prior studies have implied, and point to the need for further research utilizing community samples."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The original claim of superior outcomes with combined medication and psychotherapy was explicitly retested. Authors report no advantage for combined treatment and contrast that result with prior findings.""}"
10.1037/xlm0000491,5f2326670f333040,1,,Positive recency in delayed free recall,"Tzeng, OJL",1973,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Tzeng, OJL"", ""year"": ""1973"", ""title"": ""Positive recency in delayed free recall"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Given that previous studies (e.g. Tzeng, 1973 ; Bjork & Whitten, 1974 ) found mixed results, we reexamined the negative-recency effect in final-free recall following both CDFR lists and DFR lists in which there was no inter-item distractor."", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": """", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors reexamine the prior CDFR findings jointly, but say only that previous studies had mixed results. They do not identify Tzeng’s original negative-recency result separately, so its agreement with the present robust negative recency cannot be determined.""}"
10.1037/xlm0000491,5f2326670f333040,2,,Recency-sensitive retrieval processes in long-term free recall,"Bjork, RA; Whitten, WB",1974,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Bjork, RA; Whitten, WB"", ""year"": ""1974"", ""title"": ""Recency-sensitive retrieval processes in long-term free recall"", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Given that previous studies (e.g. Tzeng, 1973 ; Bjork & Whitten, 1974 ) found mixed results, we reexamined the negative-recency effect in final-free recall following both CDFR lists and DFR lists in which there was no inter-item distractor."", ""outcome"": ""cannot_be_determined"", ""outcome_quote"": """", ""outcome_quote_section"": """", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The prior CDFR studies are jointly described as yielding mixed results without assigning individual findings. Present negative recency is clear, but agreement with this specific original is not established in the supplied article.""}"
10.1002/jeab.169,b14202f6b448d3d9,1,10.1016/0031-9384(93)90191-h,Odor matching and odor memory in the rat.,"Lu XM, Slotnick BM, Silberberg AM.",1993,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Lu XM, Slotnick BM, Silberberg AM."", ""year"": ""1993"", ""title"": ""Odor matching and odor memory in the rat."", ""doi"": ""10.1016/0031-9384(93)90191-h"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""In summary, Experiment 2 replicated the findings of Lu et al. (1993) in showing that rats can acquire identity matching using a successive discrimination procedure with odor stimuli, and extended their findings to demonstrate generalized identity matching to novel odor stimuli using unreinforced probe conditions."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In summary, Experiment 2 replicated the findings of Lu et al. (1993) in showing that rats can acquire identity matching using a successive discrimination procedure with odor stimuli, and extended their findings to demonstrate generalized identity matching to novel odor stimuli using unreinforced probe conditions."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""results"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Explicit comparison and verdict for this target.""}"
10.31275/20211931,ba34c6d310f46998,0,10.1063/1.2388760,Self-organization of temporal structures—A possible solution for the intervention problem.,"von Lucadou, W.",2006,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""von Lucadou, W."", ""year"": ""2006"", ""title"": ""Self-organization of temporal structures—A possible solution for the intervention problem."", ""doi"": ""10.1063/1.2388760"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""1"", ""evidence_quote"": ""In the study reported here, the choice was made for a ‘button\u0002push’ scheme, as in the studies by von Lucadou (2006) and Walach\net al. (2020), but to only use psychological variables obtained before\nphysical ones for the main analysis."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""1) The conceptual replication of the CMM-type experiment of\nthe type performed before (von Lucadou, 2006; Walach et al., 2020)\n(Experiment 1 as reported above) has yielded no evidence of anoma\u0002lous correlations."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true}"
10.31275/20211931,ba34c6d310f46998,2,,Two attempted retro-priming replications show theory-relevant anomalous connectivity.,"Jolij, J., & Bierman, D.",2019,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Jolij, J., & Bierman, D."", ""year"": ""2019"", ""title"": ""Two attempted retro-priming replications show theory-relevant anomalous connectivity."", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": ""2"", ""evidence_quote"": ""Experiment 2 is a conceptual replication of the work\nreported in Jolij and Bierman (2019)."", ""outcome"": ""successful"", ""outcome_quote"": ""2) The second experiment in this study (Experiment 2), a concept\u0002ual replication of the work reported by Jolij and Bierman (2019), yielded\nmarginal evidence (p = .064) of anomalous connectivity—of the same\norder of magnitude as found in Jolij and Bierman."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true}"
10.1095/biolreprod.112.106377,2b4faa1d0d497c42,0,,,,,abstract,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": """", ""year"": """", ""title"": """", ""doi"": """", ""identified_by"": """", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Recently, a Chinese genomewide association study (GWAS) identified four autosomal single-nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) loci as being significantly associated with risk factors for nonobstructive azoospermia (NOA; P < 5 × 10(-8)). In the present study, we performed a replication study on two Japanese cohorts from different institutions in order to evaluate whether SNP loci are associated with NOA."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""None of the SNPs was significantly associated with NOA (P > 0.05)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""abstract"", ""outcome_confident"": false, ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_reasoning"": ""Original four significant associations were retested, and none was significant. Three directional agreements are noted, but do not establish confirmation. Full discussion unavailable; uncertainty retained.""}"
10.7287/peerj.preprints.3352v1,c75e48cfc0df56cd,0,10.1002/dev.20062,Handedness and specific language impairment: A study of 6-year-old twins,"Bishop, D. V. M.",2005,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Bishop, D. V. M."", ""year"": ""2005"", ""title"": ""Handedness and specific language impairment: A study of 6-year-old twins"", ""doi"": ""10.1002/dev.20062"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""In an attempt to replicate the previously reported relationship between language disorder and a reduced tendency to reach across the midline (Bishop, 2005; E. L. Hill & Bishop, 1998), we also assessed whether the probability of reaching to the seven spatial positions in the QHP task differed between the DLD and TD groups."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""In particular, our failure to replicate a between-groups difference in the probability of reaching across the midline with the right hand indicates that this may not be a marker of compromised neurodevelopment relevant to language disorder, as previously suggested (Bishop, 2005; E. L. Hill & Bishop, 1998)."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The corresponding published association is tested in the new twin sample and is not supported.""}"
