10.31577/sp.2021.03.824,d5d12db97a6155d5,3,10.1016/j.joep.2013.11.001,Beyond Mars and Venus: Understanding gender differences in financial risk tolerance.,"Lemaster, P., & Strough, J. N.",2014,full_text,,unverified,unresolved,{},"{""authors"": ""Lemaster, P., & Strough, J. N."", ""year"": ""2014"", ""title"": ""Beyond Mars and Venus: Understanding gender differences in financial risk tolerance."", ""doi"": ""10.1016/j.joep.2013.11.001"", ""identified_by"": ""citation"", ""study_numbers"": """", ""replication_study_numbers"": """", ""evidence_quote"": ""Previous research provided support for the hypothesis that masculinity is related to lower risk aversion, i.e., more masculine individuals are willing to take more risks, regardless of their biological sex (Demaree et al., 2009; Lemaster & Strough, 2014; Meier-Pesti & Penz, 2008). However, we did not corroborate this effect."", ""outcome"": ""failed"", ""outcome_quote"": ""Previous research provided support for the hypothesis that masculinity is related to lower risk aversion, i.e., more masculine individuals are willing to take more risks, regardless of their biological sex (Demaree et al., 2009; Lemaster & Strough, 2014; Meier-Pesti & Penz, 2008). However, we did not corroborate this effect."", ""outcome_quote_section"": ""discussion"", ""outcome_computation"": """", ""outcome_computational_quote"": """", ""outcome_robustness"": """", ""outcome_robustness_quote"": """", ""outcome_confident"": true, ""outcome_reasoning"": ""The authors directly compare the tested finding with this cited original.""}"
